#usda 1.0
(
    defaultPrim = "Robotiq_2F_140"
    doc = """Newton (MuJoCo-Warp) parallel-grip physics for the Robotiq 2F-140.

Thin overlay on the shared Newton four-bar (./Robotiq_2F_140_newton_fourbar_physics.usda:
loop_closure spherical equalities, inner-knuckle springs, right_outer_knuckle NewtonMimic,
finger_joint drive, root_joint + articulation root, Mjc tuning) over the shared Newton-pure
bodies/colliders (./Robotiq_2F_140_newton_common_physics.usda) and the neutral joint frames
(./Robotiq_2F_140_kinematics_physics.usda).

This variant's ONLY delta is removing the four-bar's distal coupler DOF so the linkage is
forced PARALLEL instead of encompassing:
  * left/right_outer_finger_joint are SUPPRESSED (active=false), and
  * outer_finger is rigidly WELDED to outer_knuckle (FixedJoint).

outer_finger stays in the articulation (so the loop_closure equality, which references it,
still resolves); locking its DOF constrains the four-bar to parallel motion. This closed-loop
formulation is rigid (no oscillation), unlike an open tree coupled by independent mimic
constraints. Mirrors the 2F-85 Newton variant of the same name; only the 2F-140 values
differ.

RV.011: shared Newton+MuJoCo tuning (same as newton_compliant, from the fourbar layer) --
the mjc:* params tune the MuJoCo-Warp (Newton) solver; no Physx* runtime data here."""
    metersPerUnit = 1
    subLayers = [
        @./Robotiq_2F_140_newton_fourbar_physics.usda@,
        @./Robotiq_2F_140_newton_common_physics.usda@,
        @./Robotiq_2F_140_body_mass_physics.usda@,
        # fingertip_physics only authors values nothing else overrides, so its slot is arbitrary.
        @./Robotiq_2F_140_fingertip_physics.usda@,
        @./Robotiq_2F_140_kinematics_physics.usda@,
        @./base.usda@
    ]
    upAxis = "Z"
)

over "Robotiq_2F_140"
{
    over "Robotiq_2F_140"
    {
        over "Joints"
        {
            # Parallel: distal coupler DOF removed (outer_finger welded rigid below). The
            # live four-bar revolutes live in the compliant variant; the shared fourbar
            # layer leaves outer_finger_joint untouched so each variant decides its fate.
            over "left_outer_finger_joint" (active = false) {}
            over "right_outer_finger_joint" (active = false) {}
        }

        # Rigidly weld outer_finger to outer_knuckle (removes the four-bar's distal DOF
        # -> forces parallel). Same prim name, bodies and identity frames as the PhysX
        # parallel_grip weld (all link frames are identity/world), so robot.usda covers both. Composes with the shared fourbar layer's outer_finger
        # loop-closure self-collision exclusion on the same prim.
        over "left_outer_finger"
        {
            def PhysicsFixedJoint "FixedJoint"
            {
                rel physics:body0 = </Robotiq_2F_140/Robotiq_2F_140/left_outer_knuckle>
                rel physics:body1 = </Robotiq_2F_140/Robotiq_2F_140/left_outer_finger>
                point3f physics:localPos0 = (0, 0, 0)
                point3f physics:localPos1 = (0, 0, 0)
                quatf physics:localRot0 = (1, 0, 0, 0)
                quatf physics:localRot1 = (1, 0, 0, 0)
            }
        }

        over "right_outer_finger"
        {
            def PhysicsFixedJoint "FixedJoint"
            {
                rel physics:body0 = </Robotiq_2F_140/Robotiq_2F_140/right_outer_knuckle>
                rel physics:body1 = </Robotiq_2F_140/Robotiq_2F_140/right_outer_finger>
                point3f physics:localPos0 = (0, 0, 0)
                point3f physics:localPos1 = (0, 0, 0)
                quatf physics:localRot0 = (1, 0, 0, 0)
                quatf physics:localRot1 = (1, 0, 0, 0)
            }
        }
    }
}
